-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",124,{
[3937]="7004DB08\n1\tDefeat aurochs in the Dale-lands (total: 10)\030Defeat Thrumtróth the Thunderer\tThrumtróth the Thunderer and other aurochs can be found in the wilderness of the Dale-lands. You should hunt aurochs and Thrumtróth the Thunderer.\n2\tTalk to Rékar\tRékar the Huntsman can be found in Dale. You should talk to Rékar.\n",
[3938]="7004DB09\n1\tDefeat northern river-avanc (total: 10)\030Defeat Fenskin\tNorthern river-avanc and Fenskin can be found in the Marshes in the Dale-lands. You should hunt northern river-avanc and Fenskin.\n2\tTalk to Rékar\tRékar the Huntsman can be found in Dale. You should talk to Rékar.\n",
[3939]="7004DB0B\n1\tDefeat mountain lynxes (total: 10)\030Defeat Snowfell\tMountain lynxes and Snowfell can be found on the slopes of Erebor. You should hunt mountain lynxes and Snowfell.\n2\tTalk to Rékar\tRékar the Huntsman can be found in Dale. You should talk to Rékar.\n",
[3940]="7004DB0A\n1\tDefeat Dale-lands moose (total: 10)\030Defeat Oakthorn\tDale-lands Moose and Oakthorn can be found in the wilderness near Dale. You should hunt Dale-lands Moose and Oakthorn.\n2\tTalk to Rékar\tRékar the Huntsman can be found in Dale. You should talk to Rékar.\n",
[3941]="70071CD8\n1\tLocate the red book 'A History of Zajâna'\tLocate the red book 'A History of Zajâna' in the south wing of the Kalmakhíla in Zajâna.\n2\tLocate the red book 'A History of Zajâna' in the south wing of the Kalmakhíla in Zajâna.\t\n3\tFlee from the Tarsâri and return to Rayíka!\tFlee from the Tarsâri and return to Rayíka just outside the Kalmakhíla.\n4\tRead the note in the mysterious book on the table\tRead the note in the mysterious book in the Kalmakhíla.\n5\tFind a man dressed in yellow in the Court of Larinâsta\tFind a man dressed in yellow in the Court of Larinâsta in Zajâna.\n",
[3942]="70022744\n1\tDefeat gwiber near gwiber-nests (total: 10)\tGwiber-nests can be found in the eastern reaches of Thrór's Coomb, south of Zudrugund. Frithgeir has asked you to defeat any gwiber that you encounter near their nests.\n2\tTalk to Frithgeir at Zudrugund\tFrithgeir is at Zudrugund, north of the gwiber-nests. You should return to Frithgeir and let him know that you have been able to defeat a number of gwiber in Thrór's Coomb.\n",
[3943]="7002C60E\n1\tRescue Darfi\tYou should find Darfi the dwarf and help him get back to the mill. Armund said he was headed north-west of the sawmill to size up some lumber-stands for cutting.\n2\tTalk to Darfi\tYou should speak with Darfi at the Limlight Gorge sawmill.\n",
[3944]="7002A827\n1\tUse the ballistae to goad Dargnákh into a rampage\tUse the ballistae to goad Dargnákh into a rampage.\n2\tUse the torches to set the Orc's powder alight and drive Dargnákh from the outbuildings\tDrive Dargnákh from the outbuildings by setting him aflame with the torches on the walls.\n3\tDefeat Huva\tDefeat Huva, an acolyte of Saruman.\n4\tUse food to lure Dargnákh to escape and continue his rampage\tUse food to lure Dargnákh to escape and continue his rampage.\n5\tDefeat Dargnákh the troll before he escapes into the wild.\t\n",
[3945]="7002BDB5\n1\tUse the ballistae to goad Dargnákh into a rampage\tUse the ballistae to goad Dargnákh into a rampage.\n2\tUse the torches on the walls to set Dargnákh aflame and drive him from the outbuildings\tDrive Dargnákh from the outbuildings by setting him aflame with the torches on the walls.\n3\tDefeat Huva\tDefeat Huva, an acolyte of Saruman.\n4\tUse food to lure Dargnákh to escape and continue his rampage\tUse food to lure Dargnákh to escape and continue his rampage.\n5\tDefeat Dargnákh\tDefeat Dargnákh the troll before he escapes into the wild.\n",
[3946]="7002BD17\n1\tDrive Dargnákh onward to his death... and the deaths of Saruman's lackeys.\t\n",
[3947]="70062B18\n1\tDefeat spiders in Cobshollow (total: 12)\tNuddo tells you that the spiders have begun attacking ever since the shadow strode through the land. Cobshollow can be found to the south-west. You can take the road heading south out of Lintrev and across the bridge. Travel to Cobshollow and contain the spider infestation.\n2\tTalk to Nuddo\tNuddo should hear about the growing infestation. Nuddo Sutchic is waiting in Lintrev.\n3\tDefeat the corrupted spider queen\tNuddo Sutchic has tasked you with finding and defeating the corrupted spider queen. Travel back to Cobshollow to the south-west and find the queen.\n4\tTalk to Nuddo Sutchic\tYou defeated the corrupted spider queen. You should tell Nuddo in Lintrev the good news.\n",
[3948]="7005B192\n1\tTravel to Ashmargathâl\tDwarves of the Kámbrada, Zhélruka, and Abnúzhu can be found at Ashmargathâl, far to the north of Amdân on the slopes of Bundushâthur. Dáin has asked you to travel to Ashmargathâl and aid the Dwarves of the Haban'akkâ.\n2\tTalk to King Shâlim Nightcloak\030Talk to King Usk\030Talk to King Vélat\tKing Shâlim Nightcloak, King Usk, and King Vélat can be found at Ashmargathâl. You have arrived at Ashmargathâl. You should speak to the Kings of the Kámbrada, Zhélruka, and Abnúzhu leading the assault on Atrad-zarakh.\n3\tScout Târ-kútoz\tTâr-kútoz can be found to the west of Ashmargathâl. The Kings of the Kámbrada, Zhélruka, and Abnúzhu have asked you to scout Târ-kútoz and defeat Azog's forces at Atrad-zarakh.\n4\tDefeat goblins at Târ-kútoz and Atrad-zarakh (total: 12)\030Defeat bats at Târ-kútoz and Atrad-zarakh (total: 8)\030Collect trophy-bones (total: 7)\tGoblins and bats can be found at Târ-kútoz and within the warding-spire of Atrad-zarakh. Trophy-bones can be collected from Orcs and some goblins. You should aid the Kámbrada, Zhélruka, and Abnúzhu by defeating the goblins and bats dwelling at Târ-kútoz. You should also collect trophy-bones for the Haban'akkâ.\n5\tRaise a banner of the Haban'akkâ of Thráin at Atrad-zarakh\tYou have done much to hinder Azog's forces at Târ-kútoz and Atrad-zarakh. You should raise a banner of the Haban'akkâ of Thráin at Atrad-zarakh.\n6\tCompleted\tYou have done much to aid the dwarves of the Kámbrada, Zhélruka, and Abnúzhu at Atrad-zarakh.\n",
[3949]="70020BAB\n1\tBring the dark crystal to Saeradan at Echad Saeradan\tSaeradan is at Echad Saeradan, south-west of Gavar Cadlus. You should bring the crystal to Saeradan for identification.\n",
[3950]="7001EDFF\n1\tCollect Blades of Necromancy (total: 15)\tSammath Gûl is in Dol Guldur. Laegalar has asked you to recover many Blades of Necromancy from the Black Númenóreans who roam Sammath Gûl.\n",
[3951]="700173B4\n1\tDefeat dark defilers (total: 8)\tDark defilers can be found within the Forgotten Treasury to the south and south-east of the Deep Descent. Falgir asked that you find and hunt down the dark defilers watching over the new inhabitants of the Forgotten Treasury.\n2\tTalk to Falgir at the Deep Descent\tThe Deep Descent of Moria can be found north and north-west of the Forgotten Treasury. You found and slew a fair number of the dark defilers who lurked throughout the interior of the Forgotten Treasury.\n",
[3952]="70017516\n1\tDefeat the Gurvand without using the rune-stones\tThe region of the Dark Delvings is far to the south-east of the Twenty-first Hall. The dwarf Sigurd has challenged you to make your way into the Dark Delvings and defeat the Gurvand without the help of runes, wishing you to prove your worth as the great warrior you are rumoured to be.\n2\tReturn to Sigurd at the Twenty-first Hall\tSigurd is in the Twenty-first Hall, north-west of the Great Delvings where the Nameless roam. Sigurd will wish to hear if you have risen to meet the challenge he gave you of slaying the Gurvand without using the runes for help.\n",
[3953]="7001750E\n1\tShow the Gurvand's tongue to Eilíefr at the Twenty-first Hall\030Collect the Gurvand's tongue\tGurvand is in the Dark Delvings, far to the south-east of Eilíefr's post at the Twenty-first Hall. The dwarf Eilíefr has challenged you to make your way into the Dark Delvings and defeat the ancient Nameless creature known as the Gurvand, bringing its tongue back as a trophy when you are finished.\n",
[3954]="7001751C\n1\tDefeat enemies in the Dark Delvings (total: 100)\tThe Dark Delvings are far to the south-east of the Twenty-first Hall. The dwarf Geirr has challenged you to make your way into the Dark Delvings and defeat many Nameless foes therein.\n2\tReturn to Geirr at the Twenty-first Hall\tThe dwarf Geirr is in the Twenty-first hall, north-west of the Great Delvings where the Nameless roam. Geirr will wish to hear if you have been brave enough to enter the Dark Delvings and face the Nameless ones in battle.\n",
[3955]="700523F1\n1\tCheck this stage in the quest journal.\t\n2\tTalk to a Nedda Pinleaf in Bree, Ost Galadh, or the Twenty-first Hall\tNedda Pinleaf can be found the Skirmish camps of Bree, Ost Galadh, and Twenty-first Hall. Harbingers of the Dead have appeared in Skirmishes throughout Middle-earth. You should seek out Nedda Pinleaf to learn more about these mysterious foes.\n",
[3956]="7006BF4A\n1\tDefeat All-seeing cultists in Kûr Anzar (total: 8)\030Rescue first kidnapped resident\030Rescue second kidnapped resident\030Rescue third kidnapped resident\030Rescue fourth kidnapped resident\tNumûru has tasked you with freeing kidnapped Urmâkhi residents in Kûr Anzar and defeating any All-seeing who stand between you and them. Kûr Anzar is located due east of Urmâkh.\n2\tReturn to Numûru in Urmâkh\tReturn to Numûru in Urmâkh with your report.\n",
[3957]="7000222D\n1\tDefeat Tarkrîp warriors at Bûrzum Pushdug (total: 6)\030Defeat Tarkrîp skirmishers at Bûrzum Pushdug (total: 4)\tThe cave Bûrzum Pushdug is north of Tór Gailvin, in the western side of the hill on which that fortress is built. Tór Gailvin is north-east of Aughaire. Finnán asked you to defeat the Orcs of Bûrzum Pushdug in order to send a message of reproach to the Trév Duvárdain.\n2\tTalk to Finnán\tFinnán is at the centre island in the settlement of Aughaire. You have defeated many Orcs in Bûrzum Pushdug and should now bring news of your victory to Finnán.\n",
[3958]="7001D0C6\n1\tDestroy dark idols in Gathbúrz (total: 5)\tIdols of the Necromancer may be found across the landscape of Gathbúrz. Handelen has tasked you with destroying the dark idols of Sauron that stand as a symbol of his power of Southern Mirkwood.\n2\tTalk to Handelen at Thangúlhad\tHandelen is at Thangúlhad in Gathbúrz. Having destroyed many of the idols of the Necromancer, you should return to Handelen.\n",
[3959]="70015686\n1\tDefeat Raulik, the servant of Mordor\tRaulik is on the outskirts of Skrithûrz-ulíma, a Moria Orc encampment to the north-west of the Orc-watch. An Orc of Mordor has disguised himself as a Moria Orc and is encouraging Orcs of Moria to join the Great Eye.\n2\tDefeat Raulik\tRaulik is on the outskirts of Skrithûrz-ulíma, a Moria Orc encampment to the north-west of the Orc-watch. An Orc of Mordor has disguised himself as a Moria Orc and is encouraging Orcs of Moria to join the Great Eye.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated Raulik, and stopped the spread of Sauron's influence in this particular passage of Moria.\n",
[3960]="70002242\n1\tDefeat Ongbúrz Warriors at Morfil (total: 4)\030Defeat Ongbúrz Skirmishers at Morfil (total: 4)\030Defeat Ongbúrz Captain at Morfil\tThe cave Morfil is in Fasach-larran, east of Aughaire. Torquil has asked you to journey to Morfil and defeat the Orcs that killed his brothers.\n2\tTalk to Torquil\tTorquil is at Aughaire, near Crannog's ruling-seat, west of the settlement's centre island. You have slain many Orcs at Morfil and should return now to Torquil at Aughaire.\n",
[3961]="7001AF83\n1\tFind the accursed dagger\030Find the accursed cup\030Find the accursed staff\tThe dagger and cup are held in the ruins of Sâd Morangol. The staff may be carried by one of the sorcerers of Sâd Morangol. Ianudirel has asked you to collect three relics -- a dagger, a cup, and a staff -- from the sorcerers of Sâd Mornagol.\n2\tBring the relics to Ianudirel\tIanudirel can be found just south of the bridge at Krul Lugu. You should return the accursed relics you have gathered to Ianudirel.\n",
[3962]="70020C89\n1\tGwyllion's Gate lies to the south of Gavar Cadlus. Rhiain has asked you to seek evidence of the Cuthraul's presence and to banish the spirit if you may.\t\n2\tDefeat Cuthraul in the Windfells (total: 3)\tCuthraul have appeared at Gwyllion's Gate, to the south of Gavar Cadlus. Rhiain sked you to banish the Cuthraul if you can.\n3\tTalk to Rhiain at Gavar Cadlus\tRhiain is at Gavar Cadlus, north from Gwyllion's Gate. You should return to Rhiain with tidings of your success.\n",
[3963]="70020C8A\n1\tDefeat Cuthraul (total: 3)\tCuthraul haunt the lands around Gavar Cadlus. Iuan has asked you to banish the Cuthraul from the land.\n2\tTalk to Iuan at Gavar Cadlus\tIuan is at Gavar Cadlus in the Windfells of Enedwaith. You should return to Iuan with tidings of your victory against the Cuthraul.\n",
[3964]="7000839A\n1\tDestroy Tór Gailvin standards (total: 5)\tThe fortress of Tór Gailvin is north-east of Aughaire. Camran has asked you to return to Tór Gailvin and destroy the standards that fly over the fortress.\n2\tTalk to Camran\tCamran is at the centre island of Aughaire, east of Crannog's ruling-seat. You have destroyed the standards that flew above Tór Gailvin and should return now to Camran.\n",
[3965]="70030C7C\n1\tCollect fragments of the talisman (total: 4)\tYou should break the locks on the chests within Byrgenstow and search them to find more fragments of the talisman.\n2\tDestroy the talisman at the source of its creation within Byrgenstow\tYou have collected all of the fragments of the talisman. The evil it emanates is terrible. Perhaps it can be destroyed at the place of its origin. You should find the source of the talisman within Byrgenstow. It is very likely in the deepest chambers.\n",
[3966]="7000222F\n1\tDefeat War-master Ranghâsh\030Defeat Chieftain Nûlthauk\tThe Orcs Nûlthauk and Ranghâsh are in the city of Dûn Covád, far to the north of Aughaire, among the western hills. Eilig has asked you to defeat one of the two Orcs that slew his sister and so avenge her memory.\n2\tTalk to Eilig\tEilig is in the Búth Luikh in Aughaire. You should return to Eilig and tell him of your journey into Dûn Covád.\n",
[3967]="7002D7A8\n1\tSpeak to Simbi in the Twenty-first Hall\tSimbi is on duty in the Twenty-first Hall, south of Jazârgund. Simbi has sent a message to Oxi, asking to speak with you in the Twenty-first Hall.\n",
[3968]="700164C9\n1\tUse newt-toxin\030Find the first goblin-corpse\030Find the second goblin-corpse\030Find the third goblin-corpse\030Find the fourth goblin-corpse\tLeeches swarm around goblin corpses just to the west of the Rotting Cellar. Gyrgir would like you to find the corpses the leeches have been feasting upon and spread newt-toxin around them to kill the leeches.\n2\tTalk to Gyrgir at the Rotting Cellar\tGyrgir is in the Rotting Cellar in north-east Water-works. Gyrgir will be pleased to hear the leeches will no longer pose a problem to the dwarves.\n",
})
